cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Extreme precipitation return levels over Germany, replicated with Destination Earth Climate DT"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
abstract: >-
  A replication of the headline claim of Hundhausen et al. (2024,
  doi:10.1002/joc.8393) — that under global warming the largest increases in
  extreme precipitation return levels occur for short event durations and long
  return periods — using Destination Earth Climate DT generation 2 in place of
  the original convection-permitting COSMO-CLM ensemble. Hourly precipitation
  over Germany at HEALPix level 10 (~6.3 km) is retrieved for two 20-year
  windows (1991-2010 and SSP3-7.0 2030-2049), reduced to annual maxima for
  1/3/6/12/24-hour durations, and fitted with a regional index-flood GEV. The
  claim is SUPPORTED: the largest change in the matrix, +16.9%, falls at
  1 hour / 20-year return period, and the change decreases monotonically with
  duration at every return period. At 24 hours the return-period ordering
  reverses, which is reported as a limitation.
